PUBLIC RESPONSE: A. a : +, b: +, c: +, d: +, e: +

In the nectar-caffeine pollination literature caffeine is treated as a pollinator manipulating reward enhancer. The canonical expectation is that higher nectar caffeine concentration

* increases the amount of time a pollinator will stay on / process a given flower, C → F > 0, and longer flower level handling is taken to be positively coupled to per visit pollen deposition and hence to total plant/field yield, F → Y > 0;
* increases pollinator fidelity / plant level retention, C → R > 0, and higher retention means more recurrent legitimate visits and therefore more pollination and higher yield, R → Y > 0;
* has a net positive direct association with yield once the pollinator mediated routes are partialled out, e.g. via increased visitation / constancy and / or via the direct defensive / physiological benefits that are commonly attributed to caffeine in the plant.

Hence with C down in a caffeine knock-out the mediated quantities F and R are predicted to go down and total yield Y is predicted to go down along all three routes C→a→F→b→Y, C→c→R→d→Y and C→e→Y. That is the all-positive sign pattern a +, b +, c +, d +, e + of option A.  The knock-out therefore removes a positive pollinator-mediated and direct yield benefit.

